662333.6015255, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 151897, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "1b6227e1913076f57eda959da0a12625", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01PQGpuXRpmeUQ7ycLzFZ1x9", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/ideawiki && git remote set-url origin \"${HT_FORGEJO_URL%/}$(git remote get-url origin | sed -E 's#^https?://[^/]+##')\"; timeout 90 git pull -q; git log --oneline | head -2; git diff 5e2e557 HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-1200 | h…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/ideawiki && git remote set-url origin \"${HT_FORGEJO_URL%/}$(git remote get-url origin | sed -E 's#^https?://[^/]+##')\"; timeout 90 git pull -q; git log --oneline | head -2; git diff 5e2e557 HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-1200 | head -30"]], "output": "```console\nfbb4400 Brief rev. 20: P6 width ratios taken from the strata tables (block 3.8–5.6 and 8.4–14.4; original 3.5–5.4 and 9.0–20.7)\n5e2e557 Brief rev. 19: account is a hypothesis; width claim at the size measured; exploratory arm separating M-hat cost from non-identification\n--- a/Brief.md\n+++ b/Brief.md\n-4. **Inference follows the same split:** the HC0 interval's undercoverage tracks |bias|/SD, not leverage; the variance-calibrated interval is right when bias is small and wrong when it is not. An interval that is honest about the unidentified part has to be indexed to an assumption, and (P6, rev. 19) the two assumption-indexed intervals tried (ladder range B₁, cubic-curvature bound B₂) cover only by being wide: 3.5–5.6× (B₁) and 8–17× (B₂) the HC0 width, and neither does better than a uniform inflation of HC0 of the same mean width. What was measured is the width of these two intervals; how much of B₂'s width is the cost of estimating the curvature with a cubic and how much is the cost of non-identification is not separated yet (exploratory arm requested, rev. 19).\n+4. **Inference follows the same split:** the HC0 interval's undercoverage tracks |bias|/SD, not leverage; the variance-calibrated interval is right when bias is small and wrong when it is not. An interval that is honest about the unidentified part has to be indexed to an assumption, and (P6, rev. 19) the two assumption-indexed intervals tried (ladder range B₁, cubic-curvature bound B₂) cover only by being wide: 3.8–5.6× (B₁) and 8.4–14.4× (B₂) the HC0 width by |bias|/SD stratum on the block (pooled mean-width ratios about 4.9 and 12; original cells 3.5–5.4× and 9.0–20.7×), and neither does better than a uniform inflation of HC0 of the same mean width. What was measured is the width of these two intervals; how much of B₂'s width is the cost of estimating the curvature with a cubic and how much is the cost of non-identification is not separated yet (exploratory arm requested, rev. 19).\n-Headline pair: the regime map and the bias non-identification (what is predictable and what is not, and the failure of the HC0 interval where the bias is large, and that the two extrapolation-sensitivity intervals tried restore coverage only through width, 3.5–17× HC0, with no information beyond uniform inflation); C6 and C8 are reported negatives in the main text.\n+Headline pair: the regime map and the bias non-identification (what is predictable and what is not, and the failure of the HC0 interval where the bias is large, and that the two extrapolation-sensitivity intervals tried restore coverage only through width, about 4–14× HC0 by stratum on the block, with no information beyond uniform inflation); C6 and C8 are reported negatives in the main text.\n-    - **P6(1), smooth mechanisms: supported, and it says little.** Median κ\\* is 0.25 for B₂ on both sources. Block pass rule: B₂ group-mean coverage 0.990, 0.979 of cells ≥ 0.85, worst group (e) 0.949; B₁ 0.967, 0.954, worst (e) 0.882; HC0 0.70 on the same cells. Mean width 8.4 (B₂) and 3.3 (B₁) in units of τ, against HC0's 0.45–0.92 by stratum: 8–17× and 3.5–5.6× HC0.\n+    - **P6(1), smooth mechanisms: supported, and it says little.** Median κ\\* is 0.25 for B₂ on both sources. Block pass rule: B₂ group-mean coverage 0.990, 0.979 of cells ≥ 0.85, worst group (e) 0.949; B₁ 0.967, 0.954, worst (e) 0.882; HC0 0.70 on the same cells. Mean width 8.4 (B₂) and 3.3 (B₁) in units of τ, against HC0's 0.45–0.92 by stratum: 8.4–14.4× and 3.8–5.6× HC0 by stratum on the block (original cells 9.0–20.7× and 3.5–5.4×).\n-    - **What the paper says.** (i) The HC0 interval of the regression GATE undercovers when the bias is large (0.67–0.70 mean coverage at nominal 0.90; 0.15 where |bias|/SD > 2). (ii) Coverage can be restored by widening: by 3.5–5.6× for the ladder range and 8–17× for the cubic curvature bound (the second figure is mostly the cost of estimating M with a cubic, see below, and is not the price of non-identification until the ex\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "6a025eaa-4213-5239-b682-45b504d8b167", "at": 1795662332.9149346, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 151899, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "1b6227e1913076f57eda959da0a12625", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "21f457ef-c0e2-5a5a-9582-0a94a8f0d7c6", "at": 1795662332.9187446, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 151900, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "1b6227e1913076f57eda959da0a12625", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "1337fd5f-7268-5e